CRASH-27: terminate rule labels copied with strncpy

newrule() copies a rule's label with strncpy(label, Tok[1], MAXID),
which writes no terminating zero for a label of MAXID (31) characters
or more. EN_addrule adds the Rule entry with realloc, so label[MAXID]
held whatever was in memory, and EN_getruleID copied more than
MAXID + 1 bytes into the caller's buffer. newrule() now writes the
terminator itself, so a long label is cut to 31 characters, as it
already was when read from an input file.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-27_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/rules.c b/src/rules.c
index 1b009ad..7728ef0 100644
--- a/src/rules.c
+++ b/src/rules.c
@@ -702,6 +702,7 @@ void newrule(Project *pr)
     rule->ElseActions = NULL;
     rule->priority = 0.0;
     rule->isEnabled = TRUE;
+    rule->label[MAXID] = '\0';  // strncpy() above may not terminate it
     pr->rules.LastPremise = NULL;
     pr->rules.LastThenAction = NULL;
     pr->rules.LastElseAction = NULL;
